{"term":"mess","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cef6ea6db2289798a3","definition":"A thing or group of things in a disagreeable, disorganised, or dirty state; hence a bad situation.","example":"No, look, I know that the place looks like a bit of a mess but it's actually a very delicate ecosystem. Everything is connected. It's like the rainforest. You change one thing, even the tiniest bit, and the whooole rainforest dies. You don't want the rainforest to die, do ya?","pos":"noun","synonyms":["disorder","bedlam","car crash","chaos","confusion","disarray","disorder","disorganization","dog's breakfast","dog's dinner","free-for-all","fuddle","hash","hot mess","imbroglio","mash","maze","mess","misorder","mommick","muddle","mullock","muss","shambles","shemozzle","snarl","tangle","topsy-turviness","upfuckery"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e196dad4bbee7bb4bc","definition":"A large quantity or number.","example":"Messerschmidts! A whole mess of Messerschmidts!","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:773e03ca3f38a7b7b7","definition":"Excrement.","example":"There was dog mess all along the street.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"euphemistic","register":"countable, euphemistic, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mess#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be401fa999200b9